  "_comment": "ADR-0562/ADR-0615 intelligence remainder plan: finish the half-completed oya/intelligence -> registered top-level intelligence/ strangler without moving code in this authoring change. Live origin/dev accounting is 51 destination crates (18 pre-landed plus 33 from the executed intelligence-move-plan, intelligence-sinkbatch-move-plan, and intelligence-supervisor-move-plan) and exactly 78 surviving source crates: 73 `oya-intelligence-*` crates in this plan and five crates whose catalog authority names other capabilities. This plan maps the 73 intelligence-owned crates and their 73 filename-keyed catalog rows, yielding 124 intelligence crates after execution; it excludes oya-codeview-cli (catalog capability codeview), oya-collab-crdt-portability-kernel (collab-crdt-portability-kernel), oya-collab-runtime-domain (collab-runtime), oya-document-format-domain (document-format), and oya-shuffle-sharding (shuffle-sharding), which require separate future capability plans. The remainder survived by explicit prior-plan boundaries, not omission: the first plan deferred service-manifest-entangled verticals, adapters/facades needing hand-verification, and five crates whose live catalog rows now prove separate capability ownership; the sink batch moved only ten dependency sinks; the supervisor batch moved eight non-facade members and explicitly refused supervisor-app until a ports face existed. This plan resolves that face gap by assigning contract-only *-api crates to intelligence/ports, adapter-suffixed I/O/provider/transport implementations to intelligence/adapters, composition roots and workers to intelligence/facade, and pure kernels/domains/usecases plus bin-free non-I/O application libraries to intelligence/core. Evidence-based exceptions are explicit: architecture-map-app and capability-registry-app go adapters because they perform filesystem I/O; assist-draft-api, assist-draft-rest, and the bare intelligence-api go facade because they depend on an adapter, facade API, or another product app rather than defining a port; dashboard-app and rag-endpoint-app remain core because they are bin-free and depend only on core crates. Existing convention is otherwise preserved: face follows dependencies rather than suffix (as in intelligence-supervisor-move-plan and os-move-plan), and de-branding maps oya-intelligence-<tail> to intelligence-<tail>. Oracle inventory assertions: total source oracle `test $(find oya/intelligence/crates -mindepth 1 -maxdepth 1 -type d -name \"oya-*\" | wc -l) -eq 78`; in-scope coverage is exactly the 73 `oya-intelligence-*` source paths after excluding the five catalog-authority exceptions above; destination oracle before apply `test $(find intelligence -mindepth 2 -maxdepth 2 -name Cargo.toml | wc -l) -eq 51`; root-workspace observability `buck2 targets //oya/intelligence/...` and `buck2 targets //intelligence/...` must both return package targets, while Cargo.toml must retain oya/*/crates/oya-* and */{core,ports,adapters,facade}/* member globs. Neither root is a nested workspace today; the eventual executor must refuse if any Cargo.toml under either root declares [workspace], if either oracle cannot see every planned crate, or if a destination becomes excluded. Plan-shape/coverage assertions: `jq -e \".capability == \\\"intelligence\\\" and (.moves|length)==73 and (.artifacts|length)==73\" PLAN`; uniqueness `jq -e \"([.moves[].old_path]|length)==([.moves[].old_path]|unique|length) and ([.moves[].new_path]|length)==([.moves[].new_path]|unique|length) and ([.moves[].old_cargo_name]|length)==([.moves[].old_cargo_name]|unique|length) and ([.moves[].new_cargo_name]|length)==([.moves[].new_cargo_name]|unique|length)\" PLAN`; exact intelligence-owned source coverage compares sorted planned old_path values with sorted live Cargo.toml parent directories after subtracting the five catalog-owned exclusions; destination collision checks require every new_path absent and every new_cargo_name absent from the 51 live destination manifests before apply. Required whole-tree execution oracle: after shadow apply, every planned old_path, old_cargo_name, and snake-case old crate identifier must have zero live references outside immutable provenance, and every planned destination must be visible per row; Cargo path/package aliases, BUCK labels/deps, Rust use/extern paths, include paths, manifests, and specs must be checked across the whole tree, not only oya/intelligence. Current origin/dev does not mechanically bind that oracle: MovePlan.capability is reporting-only, load_plan ignores _comment, and the pre-move manifest validator accepts this plan with zero file pairs and zero crate-dir pairs. Therefore this plan is BLOCKED from execution until a promoted codemod/shadow-apply path enforces exact per-row source and candidate visibility plus whole-tree residue before real-tree mutation. All 73 intelligence-owned catalog rows co-move because reverse catalog liveness would otherwise fail. The eventual executor MUST REFUSE on any missing source/catalog row, occupied destination, duplicate old/new path or cargo name, nested destination, unobservable source/destination, unresolved whole-tree referrer, relative include/path rewrite the oracle cannot verify, new facade-core-layering finding, source/destination workspace count mismatch, non-reversible shadow apply, or failure of targeted Buck2 gates; none of those execution refusals is claimed mechanically live in this plan-only artifact. No Cargo file, lockfile, registry, generated file, or code is edited by this plan-authorship change.",
